    <string name="coach_beat_title">Beatbox your beat</string>
    <string name="coach_beat_reason">The beat is the floor everything else stands on.</string>
    <string name="coach_beat_tip1">Wait for 4 clicks, then: boom · tss · pff · tss. Two bars are enough.</string>
    <string name="coach_beat_tip2">Boom for the kick, pff for the snare, tss for the hi-hat. Keep each sound short.</string>
    <string name="coach_beat_tip3">Hold the phone a hand’s width from your mouth.</string>

    <string name="coach_bass_title">Hum the bass</string>
    <string name="coach_bass_reason">Bass glues the beat to the tune and makes it move.</string>
    <!-- "dum" is onomatopoeia from the spec's coach copy, not a misspelling. -->
    <string name="coach_bass_tip1" tools:ignore="Typos">Hum low and steady, one note per beat. Think ‘dum, dum’.</string>
    <string name="coach_bass_tip2">Not sure which note? Stay on one. We keep everything in key.</string>
    <string name="coach_bass_tip3">Listen to the beat and lock onto the kick.</string>

    <string name="coach_chords_title">Hum the chords</string>
    <string name="coach_chords_reason">Chords set the mood: bright, dark or somewhere between.</string>
    <string name="coach_chords_tip1">Hum one long note per bar. We build the full chord for you.</string>
    <string name="coach_chords_tip2">Change notes on the first beat of each bar.</string>
    <string name="coach_chords_tip3">High or low doesn’t matter. We voice every chord for you.</string>

    <string name="coach_melody_title">Find your hook</string>
    <string name="coach_melody_reason">The hook is the part people hum after the song ends.</string>
    <string name="coach_melody_tip1">Whistle or hum your catchiest idea. Simple beats complicated.</string>
    <string name="coach_melody_tip2">Repeat one short phrase instead of inventing a long one.</string>
    <string name="coach_melody_tip3">Leave little gaps. Space makes a hook stick.</string>

    <string name="coach_verse_title">Sing the verse</string>
    <string name="coach_verse_reason">Your voice turns the loop into a song.</string>
    <string name="coach_verse_tip1">Sing or rap over the loop. Headphones on, phone at chin height.</string>
    <string name="coach_verse_tip2">Start right after the clicks and keep going to the end.</string>
    <string name="coach_verse_tip3">Mistakes are fine. Try again as often as you like.</string>

    <string name="coach_chorus_title">Sing the chorus</string>
    <string name="coach_chorus_reason">The chorus is the big moment. Give it a bit more energy.</string>
    <string name="coach_chorus_tip1">Sing or rap over the loop. Headphones on, phone at chin height.</string>
    <string name="coach_chorus_tip2">Repeat your strongest line. Choruses love repetition.</string>
    <string name="coach_chorus_tip3">Go a little louder or higher than in the verse.</string>

